From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] d3d11/dxgi: eviction priorities, exception mode, creation flags, counters, deferred context 2/3

- ID3D11 Buffer/Texture1D/2D/3D (and the d3d10 equivalents) Set/GetEvictionPriority
  were stubs; they now delegate to the aggregated IDXGIResource, which stores
  the priority (default DXGI_RESOURCE_PRIORITY_NORMAL). IDXGIResource::
  Set/GetEvictionPriority were E_NOTIMPL and now work, NULL out pointer is
  E_INVALIDARG.
- ID3D11Device/ID3D10Device Set/GetExceptionMode keep the mode and reject
  bits other than RAISE_FLAG_DRIVER_INTERNAL_ERROR with E_INVALIDARG.
  GetCreationFlags returns the flags given to D3D11CreateDevice.
- CheckCounterInfo reports an empty counter set; CheckCounter/CreateCounter
  (d3d11 and d3d10) give DXGI_ERROR_UNSUPPORTED for the device-dependent
  range and E_INVALIDARG for anything else.
- ID3D10Device Set/GetTextFilterSize store the size.
- CheckMultisampleQualityLevels1 validates the flags and answers like the
  non-flag version (no tiled multisample configurations exist).
- CreateDeferredContext2/3 forward to the deferred context implementation.
  DiscardResource/DiscardView/DiscardView1 are accepted hints.
- ID3D10Multithread default: a device created through the D3D10 entry points
  is thread-safe (TRUE) as d3d10core's test expects; D3D11CoreCreateDevice
  clears it. Fixes a regression of the shared flag introduced in 2601.

Gate: test/d3d11misc-gate.sh (test/d3d11misc-probe.c).
Mutants SG_MUTANT_EVICT_NOT_STORED (dxgi/resource.c),
SG_MUTANT_EXCEPTION_ACCEPT_ALL, SG_MUTANT_COUNTER_RANGE_UNCHECKED
(d3d11/device.c).
